hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1352","Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar told us, Yahya bin Hassan told us, Muawiyah bin Salam told us, Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman told me that Jabir bin Abdullah told him that he prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a prayer Fear. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs in one group, then he prayed two rak’ahs in the other group, and the Messenger of God prayed two rak’ahs in the other group. May God bless him and grant him peace, four rak’ahs, and each group prayed two rak’ahs.”"
"1353","Ismail told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, regarding the prayer of fear, he said: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed With a group of people praying two rak’ahs, and a group guarding, he said the salutation, and these worshipers departed, and the others came and he prayed two rak’ahs with them, then he saluted.” Abu Bakr said: Our companions differed as to whether Al-Hasan heard from Jabir bin Abdullah."
